# _identity.env — UPSTREAM-IDENTITY drift oracle for the REMOTE-FRAGMENT archetype.
#
# EXEMPLAR MEMBER = hugmesh-remote-fragment (the runtime federation-bundle
# sync sidecar + static nginx). These are the ORIGINAL literal token values the
# archetype recipe carries in the READ-ONLY upstream base. NOT secrets, NOT
# tenant brand — the base's own identity.
#
# scripts/validate-repo-templates.sh renders each recipe anchor's find AND
# replace with EXACTLY these values and asserts, per anchor:
#   (1) find@upstream still occurs in the freshly-pulled base  (anchor still bites)
#   (2) replace@upstream == find@upstream                      (round-trip no-op)
#
# CLUSTER_DOMAIN is declared for token-context completeness (the fragment's
# manifest/issuer seams are ${ENV}-driven deploy config, so no recipe anchor
# consumes it today); GENERATOR_ORG_GROUP is the one live anchor.
#
# Shell-sourced KEY=VALUE (same idiom as brands/*.conf).
CLUSTER_DOMAIN="snapdragon.systems"
GENERATOR_ORG_GROUP="Snapdragon-Systems/snapdragon-generator"
